# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ENSight — extension build config
#
# Copy this file to `.env` (git-ignored) and fill it in. These values are read
# by Vite at BUILD time and inlined into the bundle through src/config.ts
# (CONFIG), so after any change you must re-run `npm run build` AND reload the
# unpacked extension in chrome://extensions — editing .env alone changes
# nothing in an already-built dist/.
#
# Only VITE_-prefixed variables reach a client bundle (the packed extension,
# or demo/onboarding.js via scripts/build-onboarding.mjs) — never give a
# secret a VITE_ prefix. The scripts/*.ts helper scripts read process.env
# directly and do not load this file at all, with one exception:
# scripts/onboarding-server.mjs (a local Node dev server, never bundled for
# a browser) does parse a repo-root `.env` as a fallback for two
# deliberately-non-VITE_-prefixed variables — see the World ID 4.0 section
# below and that script's header comment.
#
# Full setup procedure: docs/RUNBOOK.md
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Sepolia JSON-RPC endpoint — used to READ the ENS profile pointer and the
# human attestation. Any Sepolia endpoint works (Infura, Alchemy, dRPC, ...);
# reading costs nothing and needs no funded wallet.
VITE_SEPOLIA_RPC=https://sepolia.infura.io/v3/<key>

# 0G Galileo testnet EVM JSON-RPC — used by both 0G Storage and 0G Compute.
# chainId 16602 (see src/config.ts; verified live against this endpoint).
VITE_ZEROG_RPC=https://evmrpc-testnet.0g.ai

# 0G Storage indexer. Optional: leave it out and the storage backend uses its
# own default (https://indexer-storage-testnet-turbo.0g.ai).
# VITE_ZEROG_INDEXER=https://indexer-storage-testnet-turbo.0g.ai

# 0G Compute inference provider address, for LIVE generative UI inside the
# extension. Optional and load-bearing: while it is empty the content script
# skips the inference attempt entirely and renders the pre-computed demo
# fixture (a deliberate, logged fallback — see docs/E2E.md step 5).
# Discover addresses with `PRIVATE_KEY=0x... npx tsx scripts/try-inference.ts`,
# and fund the ledger with `scripts/setup-ledger.ts` before setting this.
VITE_ZEROG_INFERENCE_PROVIDER=

# Where the popup's "Configura profilo" button points. The onboarding wizard is
# NOT an extension page: signing World ID's rp_context needs a Node process
# (scripts/onboarding-server.mjs), so it is served over http. Change this only
# if you run that server on a different host/port.
# VITE_ONBOARDING_URL=http://localhost:8080/onboarding.html

# The Sepolia ENS name holding this user's profile pointer. Register one at
# https://sepolia.app.ens.domains. The text record keys are fixed in
# src/config.ts and are not configurable:
#   app.ensight.profile -> 0G Storage root hash of the encrypted profile
#   app.ensight.human   -> World ID attestation
VITE_ENS_NAME=yourname.eth

# World ID staging app + Incognito Action, from https://developer.worldcoin.org
VITE_WORLD_APP_ID=app_staging_xxx
VITE_WORLD_ACTION=verify-human

# World ID 4.0 Relying Party (RP) resources — deliberately NOT VITE_-prefixed.
# idkit v4's IDKitRequestWidget requires a signed rp_context, and signing it
# (@worldcoin/idkit/signing's signRequest()) has a hard runtime guard that
# refuses to run anywhere but Node — it cannot run in demo/onboarding.tsx's
# browser bundle, by design. So these two are read ONLY by
# scripts/onboarding-server.mjs (the local Node dev server that serves demo/
# AND signs rp_context over POST /rp-context — see that script's header
# comment) via process.env or by parsing this file directly at startup —
# never by Vite. Any var prefixed VITE_ gets inlined into every client bundle
# Vite builds (referenced or not, including demo/onboarding.js via
# scripts/build-onboarding.mjs) — that is exactly what these two must never
# do, hence no VITE_ prefix here.
#
# WORLD_RP_ID: the RP id (rp_...) from the Developer Portal.
WORLD_RP_ID=rp_xxx
#
# WORLD_RP_SIGNING_KEY: DEMO ONLY. In production, rp_context's signature MUST
# be produced by a real backend service with proper access control — this
# local dev server is a stand-in appropriate only for a developer's own
# manual E2E testing, never for anything user-facing. Only acceptable here
# because the World ID app/RP behind this demo is disposable (key
# rotated/revoked after use). Leave unset (or don't run
# scripts/onboarding-server.mjs) to skip Step 2 of the onboarding wizard.
WORLD_RP_SIGNING_KEY=0x_demo_only_never_a_real_production_key


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Helper scripts (scripts/*.ts) — NOT loaded from this file
#
# The scripts read process.env directly; this project has no dotenv. Export
# these inline for the single command, e.g.
#   PRIVATE_KEY=0x... AMOUNT=4 npx tsx scripts/setup-ledger.ts
#
# Listed here for reference only — do NOT uncomment them, and never paste a
# real private key into a file. See docs/RUNBOOK.md for when each is needed.
#
#   PRIVATE_KEY       testnet wallet key (0x...). setup-ledger / try-inference
#                     / try-storage need OG on 0G Galileo; try-ens needs
#                     Sepolia ETH and must own or manage VITE_ENS_NAME.
#   AMOUNT            setup-ledger only: OG to fund the 0G Compute ledger with
#                     (>= 3 to create it; use 4 to also cover a provider
#                     sub-account).
#   PROVIDER_ADDRESS  try-inference only: 0G Compute inference provider. Run
#                     the script without it to list the available providers.
#   ZEROG_RPC         override for VITE_ZEROG_RPC (default:
#                     https://evmrpc-testnet.0g.ai)
#   INDEXER_RPC       try-storage only: 0G Storage indexer (default:
#                     https://indexer-storage-testnet-turbo.0g.ai)
#   DOWNLOAD_URI      try-storage only: skip the upload and only re-download
#                     this root hash (retry after a propagation delay)
#   SEPOLIA_RPC       try-ens only: Sepolia endpoint (required, no default)
#   ENS_NAME          try-ens only: ENS name to read/write (required, no
#                     default — the script does not read VITE_ENS_NAME)
#
# One exception to "NOT loaded from this file": scripts/onboarding-server.mjs
# (the local dev server behind demo/onboarding.tsx's World ID step) DOES fall
# back to parsing a `.env` in the repo root itself (its own tiny KEY=VALUE
# parser, not dotenv, and only for keys not already in process.env) — for
# WORLD_RP_SIGNING_KEY and WORLD_RP_ID specifically, so a developer running
# `node scripts/onboarding-server.mjs` doesn't have to export both inline
# every time. See that script's header comment.
#   WORLD_RP_SIGNING_KEY / WORLD_RP_ID   see the World ID 4.0 section above —
#                     same two variables, just also readable this way.
#   PORT              onboarding-server.mjs only: port to serve demo/ and
#                     POST /rp-context on (default: 8080).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
